      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to substitute the given values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the expression \\(2a + 3b\\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\(a = 2 - i\\) and \\(b = -1 + i\\) into the expression:\n\\[2a + 3b = 2(2 - i) + 3(-1 + i).\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the constants inside the parentheses:\n\\[2(2 - i) + 3(-1 + i) = 2 \\cdot 2 + 2 \\cdot (-i) + 3 \\cdot (-1) + 3 \\cdot i.\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplications:\n\\[2 \\cdot 2 = 4,\\]\n\\[2 \\cdot (-i) = -2i,\\]\n\\[3 \\cdot (-1) = -3,\\]\n\\[3 \\cdot i = 3i.\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[4 - 2i - 3 + 3i.\\]\n\nNow, we combine the real parts and the imaginary parts separately:\n\\[4 - 3 + (-2i + 3i) = 1 + i.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(2a + 3b\\) is \\(\\boxed{1 + i}\\).",
