      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for \\(2a + 3b\\) where \\(a = 2 - i\\) and \\(b = -1 + i\\), we first need to compute the values of \\(2a\\) and \\(3b\\) separately, and then add them together.\n\n1. Calculate \\(2a\\):\n\\[\n2a = 2(2 - i) = 4 - 2i\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(3b\\):\n\\[\n3b = 3(-1 + i) = -3 + 3i\n\\]\n\n3. Add the results from steps 1 and 2:\n\\[\n2a + 3b = (4 - 2i) + (-3 + 3i)\n\\]\n\nCombine the real parts and the imaginary parts separately:\n\\[\n(4 - 3) + (-2i + 3i) = 1 + i\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1 + i}\n\\]",
